{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/80853-the-celestial-pantheon-a-wod-pantheon-crossover-idea","id":80853,"title":"The Celestial Pantheon: a WoD pantheon crossover idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-27T00:11:48-08:00","id":80853,"title":"The Celestial Pantheon: a WoD pantheon crossover idea","content":"First, I want to state that what I mean by &quot;crossover&quot; is that perhaps the inspiration may be good for a pantheon. Second, since Onyx Path is considering making werewolves a viable PC race in Scion 2E, this may be doable.<br /> <br /> I bet a lot of people remember the Celestine spirits of Werewolf: The Apocalypse (Gaia, Luna, Helios, and the planets, etc.). I believe that the spirit system that was used resemble a sort of canon &quot;pantheon&quot; for that game. I was thinking that they could be imported as an WoD style pantheon for Scion. You have Gaia and the others as the Celestial Gods of the pantheon, along with the Incarna and the Jagglings as their servants. The werewolves can function as the Followers Merit with some being actual Scions of the Celestines. On the other side of the coin, the Titan realm that harasses them is called Triat, and the Weaver, Wyrm, and Wild could be the three Titans living in said realm.<br /> <br /> The formation could be Scion based, which they were avid players of White Wolf Games in the Scion game world.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think I would find it funny if Onyx Path got White Wolf's permission to use the characters from Apocalypse as a viable pantheon for Scion, but it can be doable.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-na